From: Project Luma
Subject: [PATCH] applications: add the Background Activity page (Luma ADR-033)

Settings › Apps gains a Background Activity row under Default Apps. Its page
lists every app with a background agent, as luma-background reports it over
org.projectluma.Background1: the app's switch; whether it is Always On,
running, waiting, paused for Power Saver or stopped after crashes; its memory;
and, expanded, what the agent is for, when it starts, when it last ran, its
memory against its limit, its processor use, and Stop Now. Turning off an app
people rely on asks first and says what they will miss ("You won't get
messages or calls while Messages is closed"), and the row keeps saying so
while it is off. "Show Only Running" filters the list. Resource use is read
only while the page is shown.

The page changes nothing itself: every switch and Stop Now is a request to
the service, and the rows are redrawn from its answer and its AgentChanged
signal. Without the service the page says background activity is unavailable.

The existing per-app "Run in Background" switch for sandboxed apps keeps
writing the portal permission store, which luma-background follows.

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
